# Magento PWA Studio / Venia — Conventions

## Override Resolution
- `src/targets/local-intercept.js` registers `VeniaResolverPlugin` for `@magento/venia-ui/lib`, `@magento/peregrine/lib`, `@magento/pagebuilder/lib` → resolves to `src/overrides/<package>/...` when a mirrored file exists (mirror the `lib/` tree from `node_modules`).
- Root `local-intercept.js` is a stub; real taps live under `src/targets/`.
- Keep imports as `@magento/...` so the resolver can swap in overrides.
- In a component override, import the **local** `./component.module.css`, not the CSS path inside `node_modules`.

## Path Aliases
- `@/` → `src`, plus `@components`, `@utils`, `@hooks`, `@talons`, `@overrides`, `@i18n`. Prefer `@/...` for app code.

## Intercept Patterns
- Targetables: replace a default export via `esModule().spliceSource(...)`; inject providers into `App/contextProvider.js` via `reactComponent().insertBeforeSource(...)`. `spliceSource` `remove` is a character length; forward-slash absolute paths.
- `routes.tap` for custom routes (`require.resolve('../components/...')`; route components go in `src/components/`, not `overrides/`).
- `customContentTypes.tap` for Page Builder types pointing at `src/overrides/pagebuilder/...`.

## Feature Layout
- `src/components/` — new screens/features (not under `overrides/` unless replacing Venia).
- `src/talons/` — talons + `.gql.js` for new behavior.
- `src/overrides/peregrine/` — forked core talons. `src/overrides/venia-ui/` — forked UI. `src/overrides/pagebuilder/` — content types.
- `src/contexts/` — app-level providers.

## Component & Copy Rules (always)
- **All user-facing text goes through react-intl** — `<FormattedMessage />` or `formatMessage({ id, defaultMessage })`. No bare literals in JSX text, `alt`, `aria-label`, `placeholder`, `title`.
- **One component per file.** Never declare multiple React components in a single file.
- **Split when it grows** — extract sub-components into their own files.
- **Logic lives in talons/hooks, components stay presentational** — move queries/callbacks/non-trivial state into a `use*` hook (`src/talons/...` or a Peregrine override); keep JSX thin.
- **DRY** — extract repeated logic into a shared function/util; reuse `src/utils/` helpers before adding new ones.
- **Responsive by default** — every UI change must work at mobile AND desktop; when adjusting one breakpoint, verify the other still holds.
- **Surface API errors inline** — render server/mutation errors under the relevant form field, not only as a toast or `console.error`.

## i18n
- Catalog at `src/i18n/en_US.json` (alias `@i18n`). With the Field `Message` override, validators return `{ id, defaultMessage }`, not strings. Keep strings statically extractable.

## Tailwind in CSS Modules
- Separator is `_` (e.g. `md_pt-10`). Use `composes: ... from global`. Theme extends `@magento/pwa-theme-venia`.
- **Don't assume a stock Tailwind class exists** — the preset omits many (e.g. `duration-*` → `The duration-150 class does not exist`); verify in `theme.js` or define in an `@layer`.
- **Never `@apply` a utility inside a class of the same name** (e.g. `.grid { @apply grid }`) — circular dependency, build fails.
- **Use theme colors from `theme.js`** (e.g. `primary`, `black-light`), not the default Tailwind palette (`gray-700`, etc.).

## Loading States
- Prefer a **shimmer skeleton that mirrors the real page/section layout** while an API loads (match structure + spacing so the layout doesn't jump). Avoid `fullPageLoadingIndicator`.
- Applies to **any async-populated UI** (modals, sections), not just initial load — never render an empty shell while fetching.

## Icons
- New icons in `src/components/Icons/` as inline-SVG React components. **No `react-feather`**. From Figma: clone the SVG into a JS icon component, do not substitute a library icon.

## Build / Node
- Production build may need `NODE_OPTIONS=--openssl-legacy-provider`.
- **`??` / `?.` fail in buildbus-babel-processed files** — notably `src/overrides/**` and `src/talons/**` (`Module parse failed: Unexpected token`). Use explicit checks and `||` there.
